	<h2 class="title" style="font-size: x-large">Karwa Chauth Puja</h2>
	<div class="entry-content clearfix">
					<a href="#">
				<img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/createweb/Karwa-Chauth-Images/KarwaChauthCelebration (1).jpg" class="thumb alignleft" alt="Karwa Chauth Puja" height="140" width="140" />			</a>
                   <p>
                   
                       Karwa chauth Puja  Thali is decorated. It is a very important part of puja done on  
                       Karvea Chauth day. It is also known as Baya Thali, which contains roli, 
                       Vermilion, holy water, dried fruits such as almonds, cashews, pista, clay pots, 
                       diyas and various types of Indian sweets in their respective Katori. The Thali is well decorated like Rangoli. 
                        The art of creating attractive Puja Thalis may also 
                       include the decoration and ritual as Alpana Rangoli. Puja thali can be decorated 
                       with floral designs using flowers, leaves, colors and also with multicolored 
                       pulses.
                   
                    </p>
                    <p>
                   
                        On this day, Gaura Ma or goddess Parvati worshiped by married women. Married women sit Gaura MA 
                        and pray for her for comfort and longevity of their husbands. A small pitcher or 
                        Karvea with water is placed in the middle. While the story is narrated, ladies 
                        circulate their decorated Thalis Baya. After Puja Thali this information to the 
                        eldest members of the family who blesses the woman with all the happiness in 
                        life.
                   
                    </p>
